  "question": {
    "text": "In a non-right-angled triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">,</mo><mi>r</mi></math> denote the lengths of the sides opposite to the angles at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></math> respectively. The median from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> meets the side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the perpendicular from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> meets the side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>E</mi></math> intersect at <math><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> and the radius of the circumcircle of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math> equals <math><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then which of the following options is/are correct?",
    "image": null
  },
